body:
Thank you @JamesMowery for your recap! I've also read the threads and, if I understand correctly, there are lots of things to consider, many of which are outside of our control. Because of this, if you'll excuse me, I'll avoid the nature and architectural background of hyprland's hack per-se.

The main method to make an auxiliary window is to parent it to another. There's also a new modal hint protocol as mentioned above but I think that it's just to add extra behavior for "you sure?" questions and such. 

After a quick test I noticed that on niri, GTK programs (e.g. GIMP) don't have this issue. I looked at the protocol dump and it looks like we set the window's parent way too late and because of that they get resized by the compositor and _then_ made "floating".

For some reason this issue does not happen on sway but niri's interpretation is perfectly reasonable and easily accounted for.

This (rough) patch fixes the issue on niri:

```
diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp
index 0126db33f2..df5602c33d 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp
@@ -775,16 +775,12 @@ void DisplayServerWayland::show_window(WindowID p_window_id) {
 			wd.rect.position = Point2i();

 			DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND(vformat("Creating regular window of size %s", wd.rect.size));
-			wayland_thread.window_create(p_window_id, wd.rect.size.width, wd.rect.size.height);
+			wayland_thread.window_create(p_window_id, wd.rect.size.width, wd.rect.size.height, wd.parent_id);
 			wayland_thread.window_set_min_size(p_window_id, wd.min_size);
 			wayland_thread.window_set_max_size(p_window_id, wd.max_size);
 			wayland_thread.window_set_app_id(p_window_id, _get_app_id_from_context(context));
 			wayland_thread.window_set_borderless(p_window_id, window_get_flag(WINDOW_FLAG_BORDERLESS, p_window_id));

-			if (wd.parent_id != INVALID_WINDOW_ID) {
-				wayland_thread.window_set_parent(wd.id, wd.parent_id);
-			}
-
 			// Since it can't have a position. Let's tell the window node the news by
 			// the actual rect to it.
 			if (wd.rect_changed_callback.is_valid()) {
diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
index 587b139e70..7a0433cb04 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
@@ -3648,7 +3648,7 @@ Ref<WaylandThread::Message> WaylandThread::pop_message() {
 	return Ref<Message>();
 }

-void WaylandThread::window_create(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id, int p_width, int p_height) {
+void WaylandThread::window_create(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id, int p_width, int p_height, DisplayServer::WindowID p_parent_id) {
 	ERR_FAIL_COND(windows.has(p_window_id));
 	WindowState &ws = windows[p_window_id];

@@ -3713,6 +3713,10 @@ void WaylandThread::window_create(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id, int p_wid
 		}
 	}

+	if (p_parent_id != DisplayServer::INVALID_WINDOW_ID) {
+		window_set_parent(p_window_id, p_parent_id);
+	}
+
 	ws.frame_callback = wl_surface_frame(ws.wl_surface);
 	wl_callback_add_listener(ws.frame_callback, &frame_wl_callback_listener, &ws);

diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.h b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.h
index 3855693581..09c51dca41 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.h
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.h
@@ -1085,7 +1085,7 @@ public:

 	void set_icon(const Ref<Image> &p_icon);

-	void window_create(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id, int p_width, int p_height);
+	void window_create(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id, int p_width, int p_height, DisplayServer::WindowID p_parent_id = DisplayServer::INVALID_WINDOW_ID);
 	void window_create_popup(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id, DisplayServer::WindowID p_parent_id, Rect2i p_rect);
 	void window_destroy(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_Id);
```

I will make a proper PR soon™ :D

Let me know if that fixes the issue on hyprland.
